SUMMARY:Applied Micro – Warn N. Lekfuangfu (Universidad Carlos III de Mad
 rid) – The Superwoman Effect of Cartoons on Gender Attitudes and Educati
 on Co-authored with Oleksandra Cheipesh (IE University)
LOCATION:Room 404\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Warn N. Lekfuangfu: “The Superwoman Effect of Cartoons on Gen
 der Attitudes and Education Co-authored with Oleksandra Cheipesh (IE Unive
 rsity)”\nhttps://npwarn.wixsite.com/warn-lekfuangfu\n\nZoom: https://uni
 melb.zoom.us/j/84741930353?pwd=1TDakj4y62yHU6dWbk6ZMFehNtmGMq.1&from=addon
 \n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nT
 o what extent does representation in mass media shape children’s gender-
 related perceptions and later-life outcomes? This study examines how child
 hood exposure to Superwoman-type characters in animated series affects edu
 cational attainment\, field of study\, non-cognitive traits\, and gender a
 ttitudes. We exploit variation in the geographic coverage of a television 
 channel broadcasting these cartoons across Ukraine in the early 2000s\, al
 ongside variation in individuals’ duration of potential childhood exposu
 re. We find that women exposed to these cartoons attain higher levels of e
 ducation and exhibit a more internal locus of control. However\, we find n
 o evidence that exposure affects women’s likelihood of pursuing STEM fie
 lds. We also find that women’s gender attitudes become less traditional\
 , while effects among men are confined to selected dimensions.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/84741930353?pwd=1TDakj4y62yHU6dWbk6ZMFehNtmGM
 q.1&from=addon
END:VEVENT
