SUMMARY:Experimental/Behavioural – Uzma Afzal (RMIT) – Arranged Marriag
 es and the Norms of Enforcement
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Uzma Afzal: “Arranged Marriages and the Norms of Enforcement
 ”\nhttps://www.uzmaafzal.com/\n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/8265440
 1351?pwd=V6TMN2ZpNRILVKO2Y5za5S7GjfbAGG.1&from=addon\n\nGoogle Maps: https
 ://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nIn many societies\, soc
 ial norms govern one of life’s most consequential decisions: the choice 
 of a marriage partner. We study the social norm prescribing arranged marri
 age and the meta-norms governing its enforcement\, that is the norms relat
 ing to how families and neighbors should behave towards couples who marry 
 by choice (love-matched couples). Methodologically\, using specially desig
 ned vignettes\, we extend the Krupka-Weber (2013) norm elicitation method 
 from first-order norms to meta-norms\, thereby\, eliciting the perceived a
 ppropriateness of various types of punishing and tolerating behaviors. We 
 also elicit personal normative opinions (Bicchieri\, 2017). We ran 30 lab-
 in-the-field sessions involving 600 men and women across 15 villages of ru
 ral Punjab\, Pakistan. We find a very strong arranged marriage norm\, whic
 h is stronger in more remote communities. The evidence on enforcement is m
 ore nuanced. Personally\, participants consider it more appropriate for fa
 milies and neighbors to support love-matched couples than to withdraw supp
 ort. When asked to coordinate with other villagers\, however\, they are mo
 re accepting of estrangement by family and partial engagement by neighbors
 . Gossip about love-matched couples is rated inappropriate by nearly all p
 articipants\, yet they regard it as fairly likely. We interpret these nuan
 ced patterns relating to the meta norms as reflecting a norm conflict betw
 een the overarching norms of support and tolerance within families and com
 munities\, and the meta-norm of enforcing the arranged marriage norm.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/82654401351?pwd=V6TMN2ZpNRILVKO2Y5za5S7GjfbAG
 G.1&from=addon
END:VEVENT
